\ Module-level value-keyed map state for the runtime-image carry. The binding is bracket-less, so
\ the map is built at module load and the word becomes a literal push the image word table has to
\ carry.
\
\ One entry's value is a quotation calling a module word. The freeze-time walk has to descend into
\ the map to collect that body and seed its callee, or the dispatched call runs against a word the
\ build never compiled.

scale: ( n: fixnum -- n: fixnum ) [ 10 * ] ;

(handlers): ( -- vmap ) { { 1 [ scale ] } { { 2 3 } [ 100 + ] } } >value-map ;

\ The declared output is load-bearing under the interpreter lock: it proves `.`'s parameter, which
\ is what lets a strict build compile the print without a fallback.
run-handler: ( key n -- n: fixnum ) [ swap (handlers) swap vmap-get call ] ;
